export anchor NationalParkStyle:
    number: 139
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: National park
    idea: Routed wooden park signs on a meadow page, with projects as arrow boards on a signpost, the week as a mileage sign and status as painted trail markers.
    base: light
    palette:
        meadow: #edefe0, the page
        paper: #fbf6e6, pinned notices, markers and the sheet
        wood: #5b3b20, every sign board and headings
        darkWood: #3a2512, carved text shadow and board ledge
        routedLine: #8f6a43, the inner groove and leader dots
        carvedCream: #f6ecd2, text on wood and blazes
        moss: #2f5a32, primary button and On track
        fern: #dfe7cf, chart fill and totals
        barkInk: #2b2116, body text on paper
        caution: #e0ac2b, the caution diamond, focus ring and overdue number on wood
        ochre: #7f5200, the At risk marker
        rust: #9c2a1a, the Behind marker and pin
        lightWood: #e3d3ad, nav plates
    type:
        Slab serif for signs uses Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Clarendon, Serifa,
        Museo Slab, Egyptienne, Georgia, in caps tracked 0.04 to 0.08em with
        a 2px dark carved shadow on wood. Body uses Gill Sans, Seravek,
        Trebuchet MS, Ubuntu. Greeting 40px slab, brand 30px caps, sign
        names 22px caps, mileage figures 30px, body 16px at 1.5, captions
        12px caps tracked 0.14em.
    layout:
        A trailhead board header holds a round tree emblem, the carved
        brand, a pinned paper notice as the search, a moss New project, a
        round bell and the user. Nav is a row of arrow shaped light wood
        plates, the current one dark wood. The greeting sits beside a
        caution diamond and line, opposite a mileage sign board listing the
        four numbers with dotted leaders. Projects hang as six arrow boards
        on a tall post, each with the carved name and category, a cream
        status marker, ten blazes for progress with percent and tasks, and
        the due date. Below are a Ranger log board holding pinned paper and
        a Trail profile board with an elevation style line chart and a flag
        on the best day. On small screens arrow boards stack their facts.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 12px between signs, 20 to 24px inside boards, 32px between sections.
    density: Medium. One project per arrow board, facts read across.
    corners: 8px boards, 4px paper and markers, arrow boards end in a pointed tip.
    borders: A routed groove, a 2px lighter line set 5px inside each board, dashed lines on paper.
    shadows: A 4px solid dark wood ledge under boards and 2px under pinned paper.
    icons: Painted trail markers on cream plates. Up arrow On track, triangle with a bar At risk, crossed sticks Behind, yellow caution diamond for overdue.
    focus: A 3px caution yellow outline offset 3px ringed by dark wood. Nav plates drop their arrow clip while focused.
    tone: Ranger plain speech, such as Trails, Ranger log, Trail profile, Caution and the trail ahead.
